      "cues": [
        {
          "kind": "chapter",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 22.5,
          "title": "A small code. A living world.",
          "body": "Inside your cells, genetic instructions become the proteins that help life work.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_0_chapter",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "start": 1,
          "end": 22.5,
          "title": "DNA",
          "body": "Deoxyribonucleic acid stores genetic instructions in a sequence of chemical bases.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_0_card_0",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "start": 1,
          "end": 22.5,
          "title": "Packed into chromosomes",
          "body": "In human cells, DNA is organized into chromosomes. Most cells keep these chromosomes inside a nucleus.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_0_card_1",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "caption",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 22.5,
          "body": "DNA stores genetic information. Cells use a working copy of that information to build proteins.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_0_caption",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "narration",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 22.5,
          "body": "DNA stores genetic information. Cells use a working copy of that information to build proteins.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_0_narration",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "chapter",
          "start": 22.5,
          "end": 45,
          "title": "Transcription: make a copy",
          "body": "The cell copies a gene into messenger RNA. The DNA remains in place.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_1_chapter",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "start": 23.5,
          "end": 45,
          "title": "Messenger RNA",
          "body": "Messenger RNA, or mRNA, carries a copy of genetic instructions to a ribosome.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_1_card_0",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "start": 23.5,
          "end": 45,
          "title": "The transcription step",
          "body": "Read the National Human Genome Research Institute glossary.",
          "url": "https://www.genome.gov/genetics-glossary/Transcription",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_1_card_1",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "caption",
          "start": 22.5,
          "end": 45,
          "body": "During transcription, RNA polymerase uses one DNA strand as a template to make RNA.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_1_caption",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "narration",
          "start": 22.5,
          "end": 45,
          "body": "During transcription, RNA polymerase uses one DNA strand as a template to make RNA.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_1_narration",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "chapter",
          "start": 45,
          "end": 67.5,
          "title": "Translation: build a protein",
          "body": "A ribosome reads the message, three bases at a time. Amino acids join into a chain.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_2_chapter",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "fact",
          "start": 46,
          "end": 67.5,
          "title": "The ribosome reads in threes",
          "body": "Each codon contains three RNA bases. Most codons specify an amino acid; some signal a stop.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_2_card_0",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "warning",
          "start": 46,
          "end": 67.5,
          "title": "DNA does not turn into protein",
          "body": "Information is copied and interpreted. The DNA molecule itself does not become a protein.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_2_card_1",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "start": 46,
          "end": 67.5,
          "title": "Translation, explained",
          "body": "National Human Genome Research Institute, genetics glossary.",
          "url": "https://www.genome.gov/genetics-glossary/Translation",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_2_card_2",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "caption",
          "start": 45,
          "end": 67.5,
          "body": "The ribosome reads RNA codons. Transfer RNA brings amino acids, which link together to form a protein.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_2_caption",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "narration",
          "start": 45,
          "end": 67.5,
          "body": "The ribosome reads RNA codons. Transfer RNA brings amino acids, which link together to form a protein.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_2_narration",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "chapter",
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 90,
          "title": "One message. Many outcomes.",
          "body": "The amino acid chain folds into a working protein. Changes in DNA can sometimes change that outcome.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_3_chapter",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "caption",
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 90,
          "body": "A protein is a chain of amino acids that folds into a shape. DNA changes may affect proteins, but many changes do not.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_3_caption",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "narration",
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 90,
          "body": "A protein is a chain of amino acids that folds into a shape. DNA changes may affect proteins, but many changes do not.",
          "id": "build_npdlzg_3_narration",
          "provenance": {
            "createdBy": "agent",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:00:00.000Z"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "quiz",
          "start": 82,
          "end": 90,
          "title": "Check your understanding",
          "quiz": {
            "question": "What carries a gene's message to the ribosome?",
            "options": [
              "Messenger RNA",
              "The entire chromosome",
              "A finished protein"
            ],
            "answerIndex": 0,
            "explanation": "Messenger RNA carries the copied message. The ribosome uses it to assemble a protein."
          },
          "id": "build_npdlzg_3_quiz",
          "provenance": {
